And yet, with my experiments, I see an extremely high rate of compliance. So in some of the lottery experiments that I'm describing to you, I see rates of compliance of 85% or over. And this is what researchers call a ceiling effect, and that is very hard to get higher compliance. So when I get asked, like, do you think we'll see different results in different countries? well, if we're getting such high compliance in the U.S., then I'm not sure that we're going to sort of see higher compliance elsewhere. And so I really do think we in America think that we are more defiant than we actually are and that we have possessed more agency than we actually display.
然而，在我的实验中，我看到了极高的顺从率。因此，在我向你描述的一些彩票实验中，我看到顺从率高达 85% 甚至更高。这就是研究人员所说的“天花板效应”（ceiling effect），要获得更高的顺从度非常困难。因此，当有人问我：你认为我们在不同国家的实验中会看到不同的结果吗？嗯，如果我们能在美国得到如此高的顺从度，那么我不敢确定我们在其他地方会看到更高的顺从度。因此，我确实认为我们美国人认为自己比实际表现得更具反叛精神，我们拥有的自主性也比实际展现出来的更多。

